@author "Claude (Anthropic)"

; The lower layer is joined to .c's layer by the first fold, along a hinge
; off the axis of the second. A hinge off the axis cannot be torn, so the
; moving set of `up to .c` takes the lower layer too, and both layers fold.
paper square
fold (map .d onto .a)
fold (map .c onto .d) (up to .c)

; assert faces = 4
; assert steps = 2
